    "title": "DA Drops Murder Case Against Austin Cop, Trades Trial for Training Gig - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Mitchell ,\n1 days ago Travis County prosecutors are moving to dismiss murder and deadly-conduct charges against Austin police Officer Karl Krycia in the 2019 on-duty shooting that killed Mauris DeSilva. Instead of facing trial, Krycia would avoid prosecution under an agreement that would put him in a training role teaching other officers. Reported late Monday, the move has already reignited debate in Austin over accountability for on-duty shootings and whether a classroom can stand in for a courtroom. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
